constants: c=2.99792458e8  Lambda=1.0890e-52  a0=9.36e-11 (canonical)  a0_alt=1.13e-10  GM_sun=1.32712440018e20  AU=1.495978707e11
           B_E = 3.66e-14 m/s^2 (Sereno & Jetzer 2006, 2 sigma)   N_Lambda = Lambda c^4/a0^2 = 100.405845

== K1  exact large-g_N expansion: the constant term
   g_can  = u + a_0 - a_0**2/u + 2*a_0**3/u**2 + O(u**(-3), (u, oo))
   g_quad = u + a_0/2 - a_0**2/(8*u) + a_0**3/(16*u**2) + O(u**(-3), (u, oo))
K1   PASS 1                        1 exactly (sympy)        g-g_N -> 1*a0 ; quadrature -> 1/2*a0

== K2  ephemeris factor of the constant anomaly (Earth 2-sigma bound)
K2   PASS 2557.37705               2558 (=2x1279) +-0.2%    a0/B_E=2557.38  a0_alt/B_E=3087.43  ratio/(2*1279)=0.999756

== K3  exact nu(y)-1 and its tail coefficient (both laws)
   nu_can-1  = -1/2 + sqrt(y + 4)/(2*sqrt(y))
   nu_quad-1 = -1 + sqrt(y + 1)/sqrt(y)
   series nu_can  : -1/y**2 + 1/y + 1 + O(y**(-3), (y, oo))
   series nu_quad : -1/(8*y**2) + 1/(2*y) + 1 + O(y**(-3), (y, oo))
K3   PASS 1                        1 exactly (sympy)        lim y(nu_can-1)=1 lim y(nu_quad-1)=1/2 lim sqrt(y)(nu_can-1)=0 -> both tails 1/y, NOT 1/sqrt(y)

== K4  numerical tail exponent of the canonical law
K4   PASS -0.999999785             -1 +-1e-6                d ln(nu-1)/d ln y over 1e6..1e8

